      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: eastern China</li><li>Females up to 10 cm, males approximately 8 cm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Eastern China.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>In its eastern Chinese habitat the Chinese Fire Belly Newt inhabits small standing to slowly flowing overgrown waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>They can be kept predominantly aquatic, but a small land part with hiding places and climbing possibilities is appreciated. They do not like longer periods with high temperatures above 25°C; when kept indoors no heating is necessary.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Live food like worms, water insects and their larvae are preferred.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>When kept together with small fishes caution is required, since these are gladly eaten.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Females can get up to 10 cm long, while males remain somewhat smaller at approximately 8 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/cynops_orientalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>For breeding attempts the animals should be kept at lower temperatures for some weeks. They spawn on leaves of aquatic plants. The development of the larvae is temperature-dependent and quite short at 3–4 weeks.</p>"
    }
  ],
